# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — keep the repo clean
# =============================================================================
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   The old demo branch accidentally committed the entire `build/` directory,
#   including a 2.3MB libMetalDialect.a. That's a common mistake on MLIR out-
#   of-tree projects because cmake/ninja generate a lot of files. Never commit
#   build artifacts — contributors rebuild locally, CI rebuilds fresh.
#
# HOW TO EXTEND
#   Add new ignore patterns as you adopt new tools (e.g. `compile_commands.json`
#   goes here if you use clangd from a separate build dir; `.venv/` goes here
#   if you add Python bindings).

# --- build artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib

# --- MLIR tablegen generated files (shouldn't appear in-tree, but just in case)
*.inc
*.inc.d

# --- editor / IDE noise ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# --- python (for future bindings) -------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# --- Metal build products ---------------------------------------------------
# These are intermediate and final artifacts from `xcrun metal` — they belong
# in the build directory, never in the source tree.
*.air
*.metallib
